      "notes": "Your Joshua Tree backup recipe, finally, using the chicken thawing from your freezer and the pint of cherry tomatoes you have (plus 1 more pint), sized to cover Monday too. If your thighs are bone-in, sear 6-7 min a side and simmer covered 15-20 min to 175°F. About 25 min, so cook it Sunday morning with the pilaf and green beans (or right after the pool). Mix 1 tsp za'atar with the paprika, garlic powder and pepper flakes. Pat the chicken dry; season with the spice mix, 1/4 tsp kosher salt and pepper. 2 tbsp oil in a large lidded skillet over medium-high; onion 4 min. Push it aside, sear the chicken 4-5 min undisturbed, flip, add garlic. Add the tomatoes, lemon juice and the other 1 tsp za'atar; cover 5-10 min until the tomatoes collapse into a sauce and the chicken is done (165°F). Off heat: a drizzle of oil, lemon zest, parsley. Reheat covered over medium-low with a splash of water. No salt with the onion or tomatoes (pinches are unmeasured, so none). Salted light (1/4 tsp kosher on the chicken): Jami, salt at the table.",
